L-NS-08(b) or POL-NS-09(e), and does not lower the confidence cap. So the rider's claim that he 'messaged and he never replied' is accepted as fact, but silence alone does not refund a fee the driver has earned by performing the wait; the rider's exoneration route is incomplete on this record.\n\nThe traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02734-01) is MISSING (weight 0.0). It is not needed: no accumulated-dwell argument is required because the single continuous in-geofence run already exceeds the minimum, and its absence carries no deciding fact.\n\nEscalation and compensation. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: confidence is far above the 0.70 floor; no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence; the parties share no no-show disputes in 90 days; and the anti-farming counters (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d 2, against completed_trips_30d 92, a rate of about 0.022) are below POL-NS-07's thresholds of 4-and-0.08, so compensation is payable rather than withheld. Driver compensation is 80% of the SGD 4.50 fee = SGD 3.60, the residual SGD 0.90 being retained as the platform service fee. Under POL-GEN-03 the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.60 — this is the amount the ruling moves, not a second payment; the rider's charge stands unchanged at SGD 4.50. The monetary effect (SGD 3.60) is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so it executes automatically. No clause produces a referral."
